With the primary model, the dense ratio fell from << F.rev_ns_sweep_asd7ft_dense_vs_combined_ib_ratio_3dp >> at << F.g2_opm_asd_sweep_min >>~fT/√Hz through << F.rev_ns_sweep_asd15ft_dense_vs_combined_ib_ratio_3dp >> at << F.g2_opm_asd_primary >>~fT/√Hz to << F.rev_ns_sweep_asd30ft_dense_vs_combined_ib_ratio_3dp >> at << F.g2_opm_asd_sweep_max >>~fT/√Hz, and the site-matched ratio from << F.rev_ns_sweep_asd7ft_matched_vs_combined_ib_ratio_3dp >> to << F.rev_ns_sweep_asd30ft_matched_vs_combined_ib_ratio_3dp >>. We found the white level at which the median ratio equals 1 on << F.rev_ns_breakeven_grid_points >> log-spaced levels over << F.rev_ns_breakeven_grid_range >>~fT/√Hz, for every comparator in both conditions named in advance (Table~\ref{tab:S4}).

